# Private personal installation

This is a private personal skill. Keep the reviewed main source on the local
machine or in a verified private repository. Install a complete reviewed copy
only for the current user.

Use the `manage-skills` private user-copy workflow. Do not use project scope,
plugins, marketplaces, managed distribution, account sync, remote-agent source,
symlinks, source-directory registration, or source details that expose a local
path.

Before installation:

1. verify who can see the source and what private evidence is kept;
2. run exact package checks and a separate privacy review;
3. obtain user approval of the profile, clients, and exact install location;
4. compare the source and install file lists and hashes; and
5. check every active client location for duplicate skill names.

After installation, verify the host discovers `user-voice-profile`, the
installed file list and hashes match source, `technical-writing` can invoke it
for attributed prose, and no remote client or project root received a copy.
